{"uid":"cli/surface_graph.py","name":"surface_graph.py","qualname":"cli/surface_graph.py","kind":"module","file":"cli/surface_graph.py","line":1,"end_line":682,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Network surface graph reader for the LazyOwn shell.","description":"Mirrors the ``vis.js`` graph rendered by ``templates/index.html`` (consumed\nby ``lazyc2.py``), but works entirely from the filesystem artefacts inside\n``sessions/`` so the cmd2 shell can render the same picture without\nrunning the Flask server.\n\nThe graph has the same five-node taxonomy as the web UI:\n\n* ``c2``      — the LazyOwn operator station (root).\n* ``client``  — an active implant (one ``sessions/<client_id>.log`` file).\n* ``host``    — a discovered remote host (from ``hostsdiscovery.txt`` or\n                 ``scan_discovery*.csv``, or surfaced via an implant's\n                 ``discovered_ips`` column).\n* ``port``    — an open TCP/UDP port on a discovered host.\n* ``service`` — banner/version metadata attached to a port when known.\n\nData sources, in priority order:\n\n* ``sessions/hostsdiscovery.txt``        — newline-delimited IPs.\n* ``sessions/scan_discovery_*.csv``      — ``;``-quoted IP/PORT/SERVICE.\n* ``sessions/<client_id>.log``           — per-implant CSV with the\n                                           ``discovered_ips`` and\n                                           ``result_portscan`` columns.\n* ``payload.json``                       — local C2 host/port (``lhost``,\n                                           ``c2_port``) for the root node.\n* ``sessions/os.json``                   — current target OS hint.\n\nThe module is pure data: it returns plain dataclasses + ``to_dict`` so the\nresult is equally usable from a Rich/Textual renderer, an MCP response or\na unit test.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["cli/surface_graph.py::NODE_C2","cli/surface_graph.py::NODE_KIND_C2","cli/surface_graph.py::NODE_KIND_CLIENT","cli/surface_graph.py::NODE_KIND_HOST","cli/surface_graph.py::NODE_KIND_PORT","cli/surface_graph.py::NODE_KIND_SERVICE","cli/surface_graph.py::EDGE_CONTROLS","cli/surface_graph.py::EDGE_DISCOVERED","cli/surface_graph.py::EDGE_OPENS","cli/surface_graph.py::EDGE_RUNS","cli/surface_graph.py::SurfaceNode","cli/surface_graph.py::SurfaceEdge","cli/surface_graph.py::SurfaceGraph","cli/surface_graph.py::SurfaceGraphConfig","cli/surface_graph.py::SurfaceGraphBuilder","cli/surface_graph.py::build_surface_graph","cli/surface_graph.py::iter_descendants"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
